om2
note tools/tally.om: the pull counter of the Omega forge, in pure seeded Omega.
note
note Every time someone pulls a repository from my seed it leaves one line in a log: nginx writes
note one for a fetch over HTTPS, radicle-node one for a fetch over the Radicle protocol. This
note program reads those lines and keeps, per repository and per UTC day, how many pulls there
note were and from how many distinct hosts or peers. It stores counts only: no address, no node
note id and no other byte of a log line is ever written. Build with the seed-born compiler:
note   omc < tools/tally.om > tally && chmod +x tally
note   { printf 'target x86linux\n'; cat tools/tally.om; } | omc-x86 > tally   (native x86-64)
note Run:
note   tally LEDGER OUT < LOGS
note   LEDGER  read: the ledger so far. The header line is exactly
note             rid TAB day TAB https TAB hosts TAB rad TAB peers
note           then one row per (repository, day), exactly 6 TAB-separated fields:
note             rid    rad:z followed by 20 to 60 base58 characters
note             day    YYYY-MM-DD, a real date from 1970 to 9999
note             https  pulls over HTTPS that day          hosts  distinct hosts among them
note             rad    pulls over the Radicle protocol    peers  distinct node ids among them
note           counts in decimal, no leading zero except 0 itself, at most 19 digits; hosts is at
note           most https and peers at most rad. Rows are in ascending bytewise (rid, day) order and
note           each (rid, day) appears once. Every line ends in a newline: an empty file, a blank
note           line, a CR anywhere or a last line without its newline is refused. The header alone is
note           valid. At most 262144 rows and 16 MiB.
note   LOGS    standard input: any mix of lines of the two logs, in any order, read as a stream. A
note           line that matches neither pattern is ignored, never refused: logs carry bytes that
note           strangers chose. A line over 16384 bytes is ignored. Bytes after the last newline
note           count as a last line.
note             HTTPS, nginx combined format:
note               HOST SP X SP X SP [DD/Mon/YYYY:HH:MM:SS SP +HHMM] SP
note               "GET SP /rad/ZID.git/info/refs?service=git-upload-pack SP HTTP/D.D" SP 200 SP ...
note             HOST is 1 to 64 bytes without a space; the two X fields are nonempty and without a
note             space; the offset is +HHMM or -HHMM; D is one digit (HTTP/1.0, 1.1, 2.0, 3.0). The
note             day is the UTC day of the logged time once the offset is taken away.
note             RAD, radicle-node:
note               YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS(.f)Z SP+ INFO SP+ wire SP+ Peer SP NID SP fetched SP RID SP
note               from SP us SP successfully, then the end of the line
note             with 1 to 9 digits of fraction, or none. The day is the first 10 bytes.
note           ZID is RID without "rad:"; NID is z and 20 to 60 base58 characters.
note   OUT     written: the new ledger, in LEDGER's format. For every (rid, day) that LOGS mention,
note           the counts from LOGS, replacing the LEDGER row; every other LEDGER row unchanged.
note           So tally is idempotent: the same logs again give the same ledger. OUT may name the
note           same file as LEDGER, which is read whole first. OUT is written once, at the end;
note           write it to a new name and rename it when a crash must not leave half a ledger.
note Counting: https and rad count matching lines; hosts and peers count distinct HOST and NID
note byte strings per (rid, day), compared byte for byte (FNV-1a 64 only finds candidates).
note Exit 0 when OUT is written, with one stderr line
note   tally: lines L https H rad R ignored I days D rows N
note (D the (rid, day) pairs the logs mention, N the rows of OUT); 2 for the wrong number of
note arguments, with the usage line on stderr; 1 for any refusal, with one stderr line
note "tally: ..." and OUT not opened. Refused: a malformed LEDGER (naming the file and its line),
note an unreadable input, more than 4096 (rid, day) pairs or 262144 distinct hosts and peers in
note one run, and an OUT over 262144 rows or 16 MiB. The output depends only on the arguments and
note the input bytes: no clock, no environment.

note LEDGER bytes; one byte to see that a file does not end at 16 MiB
global lb uchar 16777216
global lb1 uchar 1
note OUT bytes
global ob uchar 16777216
global obn ulong 1
note the window over standard input: complete lines are handled where they lie, the partial
note last line moves to the front before the next read
global sb uchar 4194304
note the path named by the current argument
global pb uchar 4096
global pbn ulong 1
note LEDGER rows: offset of the line, offset of its newline, length of its rid; the row count
global lo ulong 262144
global lq ulong 262144
global lr ulong 262144
global nl ulong 1
note the fields of the current LEDGER line: offset and length of each of 6
global fld ulong 12
note (rid, day) cells the logs mention: ZID bytes (64 per cell), ZID length, day bytes (16 per
note cell), counts (https hosts rad peers per cell), the cell count, a hash table of cell + 1
global cz uchar 262144
global czn ulong 4096
global cd uchar 65536
global cn ulong 16384
global nc ulong 1
global hc ulong 8192
note distinct hosts and node ids: bytes (64 per key), length, cell * 2 + kind (0 host, 1 node);
note the key count; a hash table of key + 1, never more than half full
global kn uchar 16777216
global kl ulong 262144
global kc ulong 262144
global nk ulong 1
global hk ulong 524288
note the cells in (rid, day) order
global so ulong 4096
note the current log line: its UTC day as YYYY-MM-DD; year, month and day; the fields found
note (name offset, name length, ZID offset, ZID length)
global dy uchar 16
global ymd ulong 3
global pf ulong 4
note counters: lines, https lines, rad lines; rows of OUT
global st ulong 3
global nout ulong 1

text tpre "tally: "
text tnl "\n"
text tusage "usage: tally LEDGER OUT < LOGS\n"
text targ "cannot read a command-line argument"
text topen "cannot open "
text tread "cannot read "
text tbig "file over 16 MiB: "
text twrite "cannot write "
text tstdin "cannot read standard input"
text tline ": line "
text tcol ": "
text tempty ": empty file"
text tnonl "no newline at the end of the line"
text tblank "blank line"
text tcr "carriage return in the line"
text thdr "rid\tday\thttps\thosts\trad\tpeers"
text tbhd "header line is not rid TAB day TAB https TAB hosts TAB rad TAB peers"
text tcols "row needs exactly 6 TAB-separated fields"
text tbrid "rid is not rad:z and 20 to 60 base58 characters"
text tbday "day is not a date YYYY-MM-DD from 1970 to 9999"
text tbnum "a count is not a decimal number of at most 19 digits without a leading zero"
text thost "hosts is more than https"
text tpeer "peers is more than rad"
text tdup "repeats the (rid, day) of line "
text tord "is not after line "
text tord2 " in (rid, day) order"
text tmanyl "more than 262144 rows"
text tmanyc "more than 4096 (rid, day) pairs in the logs"
text tmanyk "more than 262144 distinct hosts and peers in the logs"
text tmanyo "OUT over 262144 rows"
text toverf "OUT over 16 MiB"
text tsum1 "lines "
text tsum2 " https "
text tsum3 " rad "
text tsum4 " ignored "
text tsum5 " days "
text tsum6 " rows "
text trad "rad:"
text tmon "JanFebMarAprMayJunJulAugSepOctNovDec"
text tget "\"GET /rad/"
text tref ".git/info/refs?service=git-upload-pack HTTP/"
text tinfo "INFO"
text twire "wire"
text tpeerw "Peer "
text tfet " fetched rad:"
text tfrom " from us successfully"

note wdec: write v in decimal to stderr
fn wdec v ulong to void
d = new uchar 20 0
x = v
k = ulong 20
note a ulong has at most 20 digits
while true bound 20
k = sub k 1
put d k uchar add rem x 10 48
x = div x 10
if eq x 0
break
end
end
w = write 2 d k sub 20 k
end

note diem: refuse with m alone, then exit 1
fn diem m view uchar * to void
w = write 2 tpre 0 len tpre
w = write 2 m 0 len m
w = write 2 tnl 0 len tnl
exit 1
end

note dief: refuse with m and the current path, then exit 1
fn dief m view uchar * to void
w = write 2 tpre 0 len tpre
w = write 2 m 0 len m
w = write 2 pb 0 get pbn 0
w = write 2 tnl 0 len tnl
exit 1
end

note diel: refuse line ln of LEDGER with m, then the line number j when j is not 0; exit 1
fn diel m view uchar * ln ulong j ulong to void
w = write 2 tpre 0 len tpre
w = write 2 pb 0 get pbn 0
w = write 2 tline 0 len tline
wdec ln
w = write 2 tcol 0 len tcol
w = write 2 m 0 len m
if ne j 0
wdec j
end
w = write 2 tnl 0 len tnl
exit 1
end

note dord: refuse line ln of LEDGER, which does not come after line j in (rid, day) order
fn dord ln ulong j ulong to void
w = write 2 tpre 0 len tpre
w = write 2 pb 0 get pbn 0
w = write 2 tline 0 len tline
wdec ln
w = write 2 tcol 0 len tcol
w = write 2 tord 0 len tord
wdec j
w = write 2 tord2 0 len tord2
w = write 2 tnl 0 len tnl
exit 1
end

note chk: refuse line ln with m when ok is false
fn chk ok bool m view uchar * ln ulong to void
if not ok
diel m ln 0
end
end

note setpath: copy command-line argument ai into pb
fn setpath ai ulong to void
n = argread ai pb 0 4096
if le n 0
diem targ
end
put pbn 0 ulong n
end

note loadl: read the file named by argument ai into lb; return its length
fn loadl ai ulong to ulong
setpath ai
fd = fopen pb 0 get pbn 0 0 0
if lt fd 0
dief topen
end
p = ulong 0
note every pass but the last reads at least one byte of the 16777216-byte buffer
while lt p 16777216 bound 16777217
k = read int fd lb p sub 16777216 p
if lt k 0
dief tread
end
if eq k 0
break
end
p = add p ulong k
end
if eq p 16777216
k = read int fd lb1 0 1
if ne k 0
dief tbig
end
end
c = fclose int fd
ret p
end

note wout: write ob to the file named by argument ai (created or truncated, mode 0644)
fn wout ai ulong to void
setpath ai
fd = fopen pb 0 get pbn 0 577 420
if lt fd 0
dief topen
end
n = get obn 0
p = ulong 0
while lt p n bound 16777217
k = write int fd ob p sub n p
if le k 0
dief twrite
end
p = add p ulong k
end
c = fclose int fd
if ne c 0
dief twrite
end
end

note emb: append one byte to ob
fn emb c uchar to void
p = get obn 0
if ge p 16777216
diem toverf
end
put ob p c
put obn 0 add p 1
end

note emt: append a text to ob
fn emt t view uchar * to void
for i ulong len t bound 64
emb get t i
end
end

note emu: append v in decimal to ob
fn emu v ulong to void
d = new uchar 20 0
x = v
put d 0 uchar add rem x 10 48
k = ulong 1
x = div x 10
while gt x 0 bound 20
put d k uchar add rem x 10 48
k = add k 1
x = div x 10
end
while gt k 0 bound 20
k = sub k 1
emb get d k
end
end

note gb: byte i of lb (w 0) or of sb (w 1)
fn gb w ulong i ulong to uchar
if eq w 0
ret get lb i
end
ret get sb i
end

note dg: the value of the digit at byte i of buffer w, or 10 for any other byte
fn dg w ulong i ulong to ulong
c = gb w i
if and ge c 48 le c 57
ret ulong sub c 48
end
ret 10
end

note d2: the two digits at byte i of buffer w as a number, or 100 when either is not a digit
fn d2 w ulong i ulong to ulong
a = dg w i
b = dg w add i 1
if or gt a 9 gt b 9
ret 100
end
ret add mul a 10 b
end

fn isleap y ulong to bool
if ne rem y 4 0
ret false
end
if ne rem y 100 0
ret true
end
ret eq rem y 400 0
end

note mdays: the days of month m (1..12) of year y
fn mdays y ulong m ulong to ulong
if eq m 2
if isleap y
ret 29
end
ret 28
end
if or or eq m 4 eq m 6 or eq m 9 eq m 11
ret 30
end
ret 31
end

note vday: are the 10 bytes of buffer w at o a date YYYY-MM-DD from 1970 to 9999
fn vday w ulong o ulong to bool
a = d2 w o
b = d2 w add o 2
if or gt a 99 gt b 99
ret false
end
y = add mul a 100 b
if or lt y 1970 gt y 9999
ret false
end
if or ne gb w add o 4 45 ne gb w add o 7 45
ret false
end
m = d2 w add o 5
if or lt m 1 gt m 12
ret false
end
d = d2 w add o 8
if or lt d 1 gt d mdays y m
ret false
end
ret true
end

fn isb58 c uchar to bool
if and ge c 49 le c 57
ret true
end
if and ge c 65 le c 90
ret and ne c 73 ne c 79
end
if and ge c 97 le c 122
ret ne c 108
end
ret false
end

note vrid: is lb[o, o+n) rad:z followed by 20 to 60 base58 characters
fn vrid o ulong n ulong to bool
if or lt n 25 gt n 65
ret false
end
for i ulong 4
if ne get lb add o i get trad i
ret false
end
end
if ne get lb add o 4 122
ret false
end
for i ulong sub n 4 bound 61
if not isb58 get lb add add o 4 i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note vnum: the decimal count lb[o, o+n) of line ln; refuse anything else
fn vnum o ulong n ulong ln ulong to ulong
chk and ge n 1 le n 19 tbnum ln
if gt n 1
chk ne get lb o 48 tbnum ln
end
x = ulong 0
for i ulong n bound 19
v = dg 0 add o i
chk lt v 10 tbnum ln
x = add mul x 10 v
end
ret x
end

note lend: the newline that ends LEDGER line ln, which starts at p (e is the end of the file);
note refuse a blank line, a CR and a last line without its newline
fn lend p ulong e ulong ln ulong to ulong
q = p
note every pass looks at one byte of the file
while lt q e bound 16777217
c = get lb q
if eq c 10
if eq q p
diel tblank ln 0
end
ret q
end
if eq c 13
diel tcr ln 0
end
q = add q 1
end
diel tnonl ln 0
ret e
end

note split6: store the 6 TAB-separated fields of LEDGER line ln, [p, q), in fld; refuse another
note count
fn split6 p ulong q ulong ln ulong to void
k = ulong 0
s = p
t = p
while lt t q bound 16777217
if eq get lb t 9
if ge k 5
diel tcols ln 0
end
put fld mul k 2 s
put fld add mul k 2 1 sub t s
k = add k 1
s = add t 1
end
t = add t 1
end
if ne k 5
diel tcols ln 0
end
put fld 10 s
put fld 11 sub q s
end

fn fo k ulong to ulong
ret get fld mul k 2
end

fn fl k ulong to ulong
ret get fld add mul k 2 1
end

note lexlb: compare lb[a, a+n) with lb[b, b+m) bytewise: -1, 0 or 1
fn lexlb a ulong n ulong b ulong m ulong to long
k = n
if lt m k
k = m
end
for i ulong k bound 16777216
x = get lb add a i
y = get lb add b i
if lt x y
ret -1
end
if gt x y
ret 1
end
end
if lt n m
ret -1
end
if gt n m
ret 1
end
ret 0
end

note cmpll: compare the (rid, day) of LEDGER row r - 1 with that of row r: -1 when it comes
note first, as it must
fn cmpll r ulong to long
a = get lo sub r 1
b = get lo r
c = lexlb a get lr sub r 1 b get lr r
if ne c 0
ret c
end
ret lexlb add add a get lr sub r 1 1 10 add add b get lr r 1 10
end

note lrow: check LEDGER row r, the line [p, q), and record it
fn lrow r ulong p ulong q ulong to void
ln = add r 2
split6 p q ln
chk vrid fo 0 fl 0 tbrid ln
chk eq fl 1 10 tbday ln
chk vday 0 fo 1 tbday ln
a = vnum fo 2 fl 2 ln
b = vnum fo 3 fl 3 ln
chk le b a thost ln
a = vnum fo 4 fl 4 ln
b = vnum fo 5 fl 5 ln
chk le b a tpeer ln
put lo r p
put lq r q
put lr r fl 0
if gt r 0
c = cmpll r
if eq c 0
diel tdup ln add r 1
end
if gt c 0
dord ln add r 1
end
end
end

note eqhdr: is the line [0, q) of lb the header
fn eqhdr q ulong to bool
if ne q len thdr
ret false
end
for i ulong q bound 64
if ne get lb i get thdr i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note pled: check the LEDGER bytes [0, e): the header, then every row
fn pled e ulong to void
if eq e 0
w = write 2 tpre 0 len tpre
w = write 2 pb 0 get pbn 0
w = write 2 tempty 0 len tempty
w = write 2 tnl 0 len tnl
exit 1
end
q = lend 0 e 1
chk eqhdr q tbhd 1
p = add q 1
r = ulong 0
note every pass checks one row; the row before the 262145th refuses
while lt p e bound 262146
if ge r 262144
diel tmanyl add r 2 0
end
q = lend p e add r 2
lrow r p q
r = add r 1
p = add q 1
end
put nl 0 r
end

note isc: is p before q and sb[p] the byte c
fn isc p ulong q ulong c uchar to bool
if ge p q
ret false
end
ret eq get sb p c
end

note eqt: do the bytes of sb from p, all before q, equal the text t
fn eqt p ulong q ulong t view uchar * to bool
n = len t
if gt add p n q
ret false
end
for i ulong n bound 64
if ne get sb add p i get t i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note tok: the first space in sb[p, q), or q
fn tok p ulong q ulong to ulong
t = p
note a handled line is at most 16384 bytes
while lt t q bound 16385
if eq get sb t 32
ret t
end
t = add t 1
end
ret q
end

note zrun: the length of the run of base58 bytes of sb from p, before q, when it is z followed by
note 20 to 60 of them; 0 otherwise
fn zrun p ulong q ulong to ulong
if not isc p q 122
ret 0
end
t = p
note a run longer than 61 is refused, so at most 62 bytes are looked at
while lt t q bound 63
if ge sub t p 62
break
end
if not isb58 get sb t
break
end
t = add t 1
end
n = sub t p
if or lt n 21 gt n 61
ret 0
end
ret n
end

note sps: past the run of spaces of sb at p, before q; 0 when there is none
fn sps p ulong q ulong to ulong
if not isc p q 32
ret 0
end
t = p
while lt t q bound 16385
if ne get sb t 32
break
end
t = add t 1
end
ret t
end

note dput: write ymd into dy as YYYY-MM-DD; false when the year is outside 1970..9999
fn dput to bool
y = get ymd 0
if or lt y 1970 gt y 9999
ret false
end
put dy 0 uchar add div y 1000 48
put dy 1 uchar add rem div y 100 10 48
put dy 2 uchar add rem div y 10 10 48
put dy 3 uchar add rem y 10 48
put dy 4 45
m = get ymd 1
put dy 5 uchar add div m 10 48
put dy 6 uchar add rem m 10 48
put dy 7 45
d = get ymd 2
put dy 8 uchar add div d 10 48
put dy 9 uchar add rem d 10 48
ret true
end

note dprev / dnext: move ymd one day back or forward
fn dprev to void
d = get ymd 2
if gt d 1
put ymd 2 sub d 1
ret
end
m = get ymd 1
y = get ymd 0
if gt m 1
put ymd 1 sub m 1
put ymd 2 mdays y sub m 1
ret
end
put ymd 0 sub y 1
put ymd 1 12
put ymd 2 31
end

fn dnext to void
d = get ymd 2
m = get ymd 1
y = get ymd 0
if lt d mdays y m
put ymd 2 add d 1
ret
end
put ymd 2 1
if lt m 12
put ymd 1 add m 1
ret
end
put ymd 1 1
put ymd 0 add y 1
end

note pmon: the month 1..12 named by the 3 bytes of sb at p, or 0
fn pmon p ulong to ulong
for m ulong 12
b = mul m 3
if eq get sb p get tmon b
if eq get sb add p 1 get tmon add b 1
if eq get sb add p 2 get tmon add b 2
ret add m 1
end
end
end
end
ret 0
end

note pdmy: the [DD/Mon/YYYY part of an nginx time at p (28 bytes are there) into ymd
fn pdmy p ulong to bool
if or ne get sb p 91 ne get sb add p 3 47
ret false
end
if or ne get sb add p 7 47 ne get sb add p 12 58
ret false
end
m = pmon add p 4
if eq m 0
ret false
end
a = d2 1 add p 8
b = d2 1 add p 10
if or gt a 99 gt b 99
ret false
end
y = add mul a 100 b
d = d2 1 add p 1
if or lt d 1 gt d mdays y m
ret false
end
put ymd 0 y
put ymd 1 m
put ymd 2 d
ret true
end

note putm: the UTC minute of the day of the HH:MM:SS +HHMM] part of an nginx time at p, which can
note fall before 0 or after 1439; 100000 when the bytes are not a time and an offset
fn putm p ulong to long
h = d2 1 add p 13
m = d2 1 add p 16
s = d2 1 add p 19
if or or gt h 23 gt m 59 gt s 59
ret 100000
end
if or ne get sb add p 15 58 ne get sb add p 18 58
ret 100000
end
if or ne get sb add p 21 32 ne get sb add p 27 93
ret 100000
end
oh = d2 1 add p 23
om = d2 1 add p 25
if or gt oh 23 gt om 59
ret 100000
end
u = long add mul h 60 m
o = long add mul oh 60 om
g = get sb add p 22
if eq g 43
ret sub u o
end
if eq g 45
ret add u o
end
ret 100000
end

note pdate: the bracketed nginx time at p (28 bytes are there) as its UTC day in dy
fn pdate p ulong to bool
if not pdmy p
ret false
end
u = putm p
if eq u 100000
ret false
end
if lt u 0
dprev
end
if ge u 1440
dnext
end
ret dput
end

note phttp: is sb[s, q) an nginx line of an HTTPS pull; then pf holds the host and the ZID and
note dy the day
fn phttp s ulong q ulong to bool
h = tok s q
if or eq h s gt sub h s 64
ret false
end
if ge h q
ret false
end
put pf 0 s
put pf 1 sub h s
p = add h 1
t = tok p q
if or eq t p ge t q
ret false
end
p = add t 1
t = tok p q
if or eq t p ge t q
ret false
end
p = add t 1
if gt add p 29 q
ret false
end
if not pdate p
ret false
end
p = add p 28
if not isc p q 32
ret false
end
p = add p 1
if not eqt p q tget
ret false
end
p = add p len tget
z = zrun p q
if eq z 0
ret false
end
put pf 2 p
put pf 3 z
p = add p z
if not eqt p q tref
ret false
end
ret ptail add p len tref q
end

note ptail: are the bytes of sb at p, before q, D.D" 200 and a space
fn ptail p ulong q ulong to bool
if gt add p 9 q
ret false
end
if or gt dg 1 p 9 ne get sb add p 1 46
ret false
end
if or gt dg 1 add p 2 9 ne get sb add p 3 34
ret false
end
if or ne get sb add p 4 32 ne get sb add p 5 50
ret false
end
if or ne get sb add p 6 48 ne get sb add p 7 48
ret false
end
ret eq get sb add p 8 32
end

note rtime: past the THH:MM:SS(.f)Z of a radicle-node line starting at s, before q; 0 when the
note bytes are not that (the first 10 bytes are a checked date and q - s is at least 20)
fn rtime s ulong q ulong to ulong
if or ne get sb add s 10 84 ne get sb add s 13 58
ret 0
end
if ne get sb add s 16 58
ret 0
end
h = d2 1 add s 11
m = d2 1 add s 14
x = d2 1 add s 17
if or or gt h 23 gt m 59 gt x 59
ret 0
end
p = add s 19
if isc p q 46
p = add p 1
t = p
note at most 10 digits are looked at; more than 9 is refused
while lt t q bound 11
if ge sub t p 10
break
end
if gt dg 1 t 9
break
end
t = add t 1
end
if or eq t p gt sub t p 9
ret 0
end
p = t
end
if not isc p q 90
ret 0
end
ret add p 1
end

note prad: is sb[s, q) a radicle-node line of a Radicle pull; then pf holds the node id and the
note ZID and dy the day
fn prad s ulong q ulong to bool
if lt sub q s 20
ret false
end
if not vday 1 s
ret false
end
p = rtime s q
if eq p 0
ret false
end
p = sps p q
if eq p 0
ret false
end
if not eqt p q tinfo
ret false
end
p = sps add p 4 q
if eq p 0
ret false
end
if not eqt p q twire
ret false
end
p = sps add p 4 q
if eq p 0
ret false
end
if not eqt p q tpeerw
ret false
end
p = add p len tpeerw
n = zrun p q
if eq n 0
ret false
end
put pf 0 p
put pf 1 n
p = add p n
if not eqt p q tfet
ret false
end
p = add p len tfet
z = zrun p q
if eq z 0
ret false
end
put pf 2 p
put pf 3 z
p = add p z
if not eqt p q tfrom
ret false
end
if ne add p len tfrom q
ret false
end
for i ulong 10
put dy i get sb add s i
end
ret true
end

note ceq: does cell c hold the ZID sb[zo, zo+zl) and the day dy
fn ceq c ulong zo ulong zl ulong to bool
if ne get czn c zl
ret false
end
b = mul c 64
for i ulong zl bound 64
if ne get cz add b i get sb add zo i
ret false
end
end
b = mul c 16
for k ulong 10
if ne get cd add b k get dy k
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note cslot: the first slot of hc for the ZID sb[zo, zo+zl) and the day dy
fn cslot zo ulong zl ulong to ulong
x = ulong 14695981039346656037
for i ulong zl bound 64
x = mul xor x ulong get sb add zo i 1099511628211
end
for k ulong 10
x = mul xor x ulong get dy k 1099511628211
end
ret and xor x shr x 32 8191
end

note cput: store the ZID sb[zo, zo+zl) and the day dy as cell n
fn cput n ulong zo ulong zl ulong to void
b = mul n 64
for t ulong zl bound 64
put cz add b t get sb add zo t
end
put czn n zl
b = mul n 16
for u ulong 10
put cd add b u get dy u
end
end

note cell: the cell of the ZID sb[zo, zo+zl) and the day dy, made when it is new. At most 4096
note of the 8192 slots are full, so an empty one comes within 4097 probes.
fn cell zo ulong zl ulong to ulong
s = cslot zo zl
while true bound 8192
j = get hc s
if eq j 0
break
end
if ceq sub j 1 zo zl
ret sub j 1
end
s = and add s 1 8191
end
n = get nc 0
if ge n 4096
diem tmanyc
end
cput n zo zl
put hc s add n 1
put nc 0 add n 1
ret n
end

note keq: does key k hold the bytes sb[o, o+n)
fn keq k ulong o ulong n ulong to bool
if ne get kl k n
ret false
end
b = mul k 64
for i ulong n bound 64
if ne get kn add b i get sb add o i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note kslot: the first slot of hk for the name sb[o, o+n) under the tag g
fn kslot g ulong o ulong n ulong to ulong
x = mul xor ulong 14695981039346656037 g 1099511628211
for i ulong n bound 64
x = mul xor x ulong get sb add o i 1099511628211
end
ret and xor x shr x 32 524287
end

note kput: store the name sb[o, o+n) as key m
fn kput m ulong o ulong n ulong to void
put kl m n
b = mul m 64
for t ulong n bound 64
put kn add b t get sb add o t
end
end

note seen: record the name sb[o, o+n) of kind kd (0 host, 1 node) for cell c; true when it is
note new. At most 262144 of the 524288 slots are full.
fn seen c ulong kd ulong o ulong n ulong to bool
g = add mul c 2 kd
s = kslot g o n
while true bound 524288
j = get hk s
if eq j 0
break
end
if eq get kc sub j 1 g
if keq sub j 1 o n
ret false
end
end
s = and add s 1 524287
end
m = get nk 0
if ge m 262144
diem tmanyk
end
put kc m g
kput m o n
put hk s add m 1
put nk 0 add m 1
ret true
end

note rec: count the line whose fields are in pf, of kind kd (0 HTTPS, 1 Radicle)
fn rec kd ulong to void
c = cell get pf 2 get pf 3
i = add mul c 4 mul kd 2
put cn i add get cn i 1
if seen c kd get pf 0 get pf 1
j = add i 1
put cn j add get cn j 1
end
put st add kd 1 add get st add kd 1 1
end

note dline: handle the log line sb[s, q)
fn dline s ulong q ulong to void
if gt sub q s 16384
ret
end
if prad s q
rec 1
ret
end
if phttp s q
rec 0
end
end

note scan: read standard input to its end, handing every line to dline
fn scan to void
e = ulong 0
s = ulong 0
skip = false
note every pass but the last reads at least one byte
while true bound 9223372036854775807
k = read 0 sb e sub 4194304 e
if lt k 0
diem tstdin
end
if eq k 0
break
end
q = e
e = add e ulong k
note every pass looks at one byte, or skips 64 bytes that hold no newline
while lt q e bound 4194305
if le add q 64 e
if eq count sb q 64 10 0
q = add q 64
continue
end
end
if eq get sb q 10
if skip
skip = false
else
dline s q
end
put st 0 add get st 0 1
s = add q 1
end
q = add q 1
end
r = sub e s
if gt r 16384
skip = true
r = ulong 0
end
for i ulong r bound 16384
put sb i get sb add s i
end
e = r
s = ulong 0
end
if or gt e 0 skip
put st 0 add get st 0 1
if not skip
dline 0 e
end
end
end

note cmpcc: compare the (ZID, day) of cells a and b: -1, 0 or 1
fn cmpcc a ulong b ulong to long
n = get czn a
m = get czn b
k = n
if lt m k
k = m
end
x = mul a 64
y = mul b 64
for i ulong k bound 64
u = get cz add x i
v = get cz add y i
if lt u v
ret -1
end
if gt u v
ret 1
end
end
if lt n m
ret -1
end
if gt n m
ret 1
end
x = mul a 16
y = mul b 16
for j ulong 10
u = get cd add x j
v = get cd add y j
if lt u v
ret -1
end
if gt u v
ret 1
end
end
ret 0
end

note cmplc: compare the (rid, day) of LEDGER row r with cell c: -1, 0 or 1
fn cmplc r ulong c ulong to long
o = add get lo r 4
n = sub get lr r 4
m = get czn c
k = n
if lt m k
k = m
end
y = mul c 64
for i ulong k bound 64
u = get lb add o i
v = get cz add y i
if lt u v
ret -1
end
if gt u v
ret 1
end
end
if lt n m
ret -1
end
if gt n m
ret 1
end
o = add add get lo r get lr r 1
y = mul c 16
for j ulong 10
u = get lb add o j
v = get cd add y j
if lt u v
ret -1
end
if gt u v
ret 1
end
end
ret 0
end

note sortc: the cells into so in (rid, day) order, by insertion; the keys are distinct
fn sortc to void
n = get nc 0
for t ulong n bound 4096
put so t t
end
i = ulong 1
while lt i n bound 4096
x = get so i
j = i
while gt j 0 bound 4096
y = get so sub j 1
if lt cmpcc y x 0
break
end
put so j y
j = sub j 1
end
put so j x
i = add i 1
end
end

note orow: count one more row of OUT
fn orow to void
n = add get nout 0 1
if gt n 262144
diem tmanyo
end
put nout 0 n
end

note emrow: append LEDGER row r to ob unchanged, with its newline
fn emrow r ulong to void
orow
o = get lo r
n = add sub get lq r o 1
for i ulong n bound 16777216
emb get lb add o i
end
end

note emcell: append the row of cell c to ob
fn emcell c ulong to void
orow
emt trad
b = mul c 64
for i ulong get czn c bound 64
emb get cz add b i
end
emb 9
b = mul c 16
for k ulong 10
emb get cd add b k
end
b = mul c 4
for j ulong 4
emb 9
emu get cn add b j
end
emb 10
end

note merge: OUT, the LEDGER rows and the cells in (rid, day) order, a cell replacing the row
note with its (rid, day)
fn merge to void
emt thdr
emb 10
n = get nl 0
m = get nc 0
i = ulong 0
j = ulong 0
note every pass takes at least one row or one cell
while or lt i n lt j m bound 266242
if ge i n
emcell get so j
j = add j 1
continue
end
if ge j m
emrow i
i = add i 1
continue
end
c = cmplc i get so j
if lt c 0
emrow i
i = add i 1
continue
end
emcell get so j
j = add j 1
if eq c 0
i = add i 1
end
end
end

note wsum: the summary line on stderr
fn wsum to void
w = write 2 tpre 0 len tpre
w = write 2 tsum1 0 len tsum1
a = get st 0
wdec a
w = write 2 tsum2 0 len tsum2
b = get st 1
wdec b
w = write 2 tsum3 0 len tsum3
c = get st 2
wdec c
w = write 2 tsum4 0 len tsum4
wdec sub sub a b c
w = write 2 tsum5 0 len tsum5
wdec get nc 0
w = write 2 tsum6 0 len tsum6
wdec get nout 0
w = write 2 tnl 0 len tnl
end

fn main to int
if ne argcnt 3
w = write 2 tusage 0 len tusage
ret 2
end
e = loadl 1
pled e
scan
sortc
merge
wout 2
wsum
ret 0
end
